# Release variant: single 8 MB app plus a 2 MB `assets` partition, whose tar is
# installed to the SD card on first boot. No ota_0, so no Bruce slot.
#
# This has to live in a defaults fragment rather than on the idf.py command
# line. The partition table is chosen by CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME,
# a Kconfig option, and `idf.py -DPARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME=...` sets an
# unrelated CMake cache variable that nothing reads -- which is why the release
# build silently came out with the dual-boot table until 2026-08-18.
#
# Loaded last by build_variant.bat, so it wins over sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3.
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions_release_16mb.csv"
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_FILENAME="partitions_release_16mb.csv"
